      "author_association": "NONE",
      "source_id": "comment:896770906",
      "issue_number": 3585,
      "parent_source_id": "issue:3585",
      "body": "Same issue here (streamlit ver 0.86.0), the callable function run on every session despite the button never being clicked.\r\n\r\nEdit: I was using the callback feature improperly. Following the documentation, `on_click=` accepts functions and then `args=` is where arguments to pass are placed.\r\n\r\nInstead of `st.button('Some Button', on_click=function_name(function_argument))` try `st.button('Some Button', on_click=function_name, args=(function_argument, ))`. Beware that `args=` needs a tuple.",
